Checker v2 refuses three calls that v1 accepts (ownership-v2.md §2.11.5, the record pass; #2494). The callee updates the record of its first argument and stores its second argument, and that argument is the top-level `empty` (`wholeTopLevel`) or holds it (`paramState`, `newState`): `disjoint`, approximate. The update writes a field of the record and not the top-level value, so no read can be stale. Each is an over-refusal of v2. `inline` is the same update with no call, and `noTopLevel` has a parameter in the place of `empty`: both checkers accept them.
